# Opens demo.md, adds a section of LaTeX formulae, then a section that cites
# a reference from demo.bib and ends on the reference list. Run with:
#
#   open -n "bin/Hermes Editor.app" --env HERMES_DEMO=$PWD/docs/demos/citations.demo
#
# The recording lands beside this script. The Cite button opens Zotero's own
# picker, which a script cannot drive, so the citation is typed in the form
# the picker would insert: [@key], resolved against demo.bib.
open ../demo.md
pause 2000
fullscreen
pause 600
record citations.mov
pause 800
goto 9
type 35

## Add formula with embedded LaTeX

A measurement leaves the system in a superposition of branches, $|\psi\rangle = \sum_i c_i |\phi_i\rangle$, and the weight of each branch is $|c_i|^2$. The universal wave function evolves under the Schrödinger equation alone, with no collapse:

$$
i\hbar \frac{\partial}{\partial t} |\Psi(t)\rangle = \hat{H} |\Psi(t)\rangle
$$

## Integrated Zotero for citation

Everett's relative-state formulation dropped the collapse postulate and treated the observer as one more quantum system, so every outcome of a measurement is realised in some branch of the universal wave function
.
pause 900
type 60
 [@everettRelativeStateFormulation1957].
.
pause 1500
goto 18
pause 3500
stop
